#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114973 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/id #uuid "32bd6b27-e95d-5de4-941f-309eb0bc61f1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4411" :question/problem "Find $AB-CB,$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAB-CB=(A-C)B.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A-C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-C & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 7\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB-CB & =(A-C)B \\\\  & =-{I}_{3}B \\\\  & =-B \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{3} & 45 \\\\ -81 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114974 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/id #uuid "3b1395b6-49c1-5e0d-ac94-c2d6fc242f6b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4412" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC,$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC = (AB)C = A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3 \\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3 \\times 3$ matrix that will require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3 \\times 1$ matrix that will require finding only $3$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114975 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/id #uuid "7ab158e6-4222-5cab-88a0-85ce74a7d4b2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4413" :question/problem "Given that $A, B,$ and $C$ are $6 \\times 6$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $A(BC) = (AB)C$\n\n- $A(B+C) = BA+CA$\n\n- $A(B+C) = AB+AC$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C = A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+C) = AB + AC$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n\n$$\nAB + AC  \\neq BA + CA.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C = AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C) = AB+AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284288 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b307c6c-b66a-5d39-8298-9e7eba80f467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284290} {:answer/id #uuid "84a1361a-1e8e-5442-b48f-b8c533733c45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284291} {:answer/id #uuid "a73e9be0-a15c-5e95-8efa-ac9158db8bc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284292} {:answer/id #uuid "8c675a0b-99ca-5086-8620-c9431c39b740" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284293} {:answer/id #uuid "f031a871-3f8b-5f28-bf58-220ac920e602" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b307c6c-b66a-5d39-8298-9e7eba80f467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284290} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d147b5f-6d58-5c16-b472-c51cdf38be30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284289}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0e3975d8-0204-5147-a2bf-df4657a2f13f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130449" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $3\\times 3$ matrices, and  ${I}_{3}$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix, which of the following statements are always true?\n\n- $AB=A{I}_{3}B$\n- $A(B+{I}_{3})=AB$\n- ${I}_{3}A=A{I}_{3}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $A{I}_{3}B=(A{I}_{3})B=AB.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+{I}_{3})=AB+A{I}_{3}=AB+A.$ However,  $AB+A\\ne AB,$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  ${I}_{3}A=A{I}_{3}.$\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284317 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Distributive Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6906ccdb-67bf-5601-96ad-3fad8344c524" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6906ccdb-67bf-5601-96ad-3fad8344c524" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284319} :answer-field/id #uuid "79136c64-d827-567e-8129-842c22759199" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284318} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2babf67-567f-5287-8719-752fb496e896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2babf67-567f-5287-8719-752fb496e896" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284321} :answer-field/id #uuid "7850a0bc-bc03-5bae-bd60-9696e52880fa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284320} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b93b47e-9d99-52be-bd00-730a53fe6261" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b93b47e-9d99-52be-bd00-730a53fe6261" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284323} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd042ce3-79ce-5510-b444-5bc6e8cfe954" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284322}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d3c06a29-7a18-544d-bf9a-8bad4341bcc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-319886" :question/problem "Evaluate $AC+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & \\sqrt{6} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AC+BC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $0$ | $0$ |  |\n|  |  | $3$ | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAC+BC=(A+B)C.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+B$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC+BC & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & \\sqrt{6} \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 3\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284348 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Matrix Product Using the Associative Law"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "678b2272-7810-5f56-a6ac-c62a10f854fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 18 & 9 \\\\ 21 & 7 & -42 \\\\ 8 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284350} {:answer/id #uuid "158cb1d4-a4f8-5487-99e1-767acc3a676f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284351} {:answer/id #uuid "761fb85b-7392-51f2-a63e-085c9a729140" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 42 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284352} {:answer/id #uuid "881f57bb-479b-5b8e-8d7f-0c549e81b862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}21 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 18 & 9 & -42 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284353} {:answer/id #uuid "087bc156-bdfb-592d-896a-4cca3f807665" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-144" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "158cb1d4-a4f8-5487-99e1-767acc3a676f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284351} :answer-field/id #uuid "e140af37-5d21-52b2-9992-47ed85fb2f2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "638edf80-8d70-51f1-a06b-07cfe064f004" :question/math-academy-id "q-42001" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $3$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-18 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 42 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
